  <FeaturedAnswer question="What is a driving instructor diary app?">
    A driving instructor diary app replaces the paper ADI diary with a calendar on your phone and
    computer that knows about your pupils. A good one shows your day, week and month, lets you drag
    lessons to new slots, warns you before a double-booking, sends pupils reminders automatically and
    keeps each pupil's notes, payments and progress one tap from the lesson. DriveSchoolPro does this
    on the web, iPhone and Android, and is free until 31 March 2027.
  </FeaturedAnswer>

  <section class="section bg-gray-50">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-4">On this page</h2>
        <ul class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-2 text-gray-700">
          <li><a href="#what-it-should-do" class="hover:text-brand-red">&rarr; What a diary app should do</a></li>
          <li><a href="#views" class="hover:text-brand-red">&rarr; Day, week and month views</a></li>
          <li><a href="#clashes" class="hover:text-brand-red">&rarr; Clash checks</a></li>
